anley’s Brian Nowak thinks Alphabet's (GOOGL) Google unit needs to do something to counter Amazon.com’s (AMZN) lead in the all-important “smart speaker” market, which is a three-way battle among Amazon’s “Echo” devices, Google’s “Google Home” device, and Apple’s (AAPL) “Home Pod.\" Amazon is expected to continue to have a strong first-place position, writes Nowak, and that’s worrisome because of all the ways that home speakers will be a point of leverage for the tech giants. By 2022, such home speakers are probably going to be in 70% or more of U.S. households, writes Nowak, and there will be one third more Echoes in those homes than there will be competing Google Home units, he expects, citing data from research firm Gartner.", "external_links": ["https://www.tumblr.com/widgets/share/tool?posttype=link&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Fgoogle-should-give-away-google-home-to-fight-amazon-says-morgan-stanley-1530216359%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&content=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.barrons.com%2Farticles%2Fgoogle-should-give-away-google-home-to-fight-amazon-says-morgan-stanley-1530216359%3Fmod%3Dyahoobarrons%26ru%3Dyahoo%26yptr%3Dyahoo%26soc_src%3Dsocial-sh%26soc_trk%3Dtu&caption=As%20I%20me"], "published": "2018-06-28T23:05:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-06-29T07:17:46.002+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}